    "origin": "Mutated Mammal, Normal Creature",
    "level": {
      "value": 2,
      "currentXP": 17,
      "nextLevelXP": 0
    },
    "biography": "<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">These rodents are the mutated form of the pre-War naked mole rat. They thrive almost anywhere in the wasteland, despite the number of creatures that would prey on them. They create their burrows underground, protecting them from most predators. They are much larger, akin to dogs in size, than their pre-War counterparts and are usually incredible vicious when hunting prey or defending their burrows. Mole rats live and hunt in packs, with their burrowing ability giving them the element of surprise in most situations, and a quick escape should their prey overwhelm them. With oversized front teeth and the ability to lunge at their prey with a surprising speed, mole rats are not to be underestimated. While they are most often mindless, savage creatures, some individuals in the wasteland have been able to train and domesticate the rodents as one would with a dog.</span></p>",
